        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-25T23:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So my understanding is that when you reference one of our named-gpios as a GPIO in any config that expects a GPIO, by default it expects 2 arguments referencing the ping and flags, but our \u0027named-gpios\u0027 appears as a GPIO controller because the GPIO reference is a separate property, and there are no pin \u0026 flag arguments, so #gpio-cells has to be set to 0.\nI don\u0027t know why we can\u0027t set it by default to 0 and have to explicitly set it on every instance of the child.\nI\u0027ll try some experiments - thinking about it,  the nodes under \u0027name-gpios\u0027 perhaps should be thought about as a GPIO controller with a single GPIO, and perhaps the node should inherit the \u0027gpio-controller\u0027 base and preset the #gpio-cells in that.\nI\u0027m still figuring out the ins and outs of this part of device tree.\nOthers may have a better understanding.",
      "parentUuid": "b836e99f_00004916",
      "revId": "e434b9a5c433e7267536ba9ee979aa22aefd3b98",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e139280_29996af9",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/lazor/gpio.dts",
        "patchSetId": 2
